    use vars is replaceable by "our" since Perl 5.6.0

    From perldoc vars:

    NOTE: For use with variables in the current package
          for a single scope, the functionality provided
          by this pragma has been superseded by "our"
          declarations, available in Perl v5.6.0 or later,
          and use of this pragma is discouraged.  See
          "our" in perlfunc.

    I didn't even notice that $VERSION was already declared
    with our... and given that we're requiring 5.006 in most
    places, I guess that means we should stop doing that too?

    Personally I'm not against people running old versions,
    but to claim I support versions I can't even install
    feels a bit fake.  Technically I don't even have 5.6.x,
    I tried patching it yesterday and it wouldn't work either
    (may have to try on a VM instead (or use some clever Docker
    or GitHub CI runner (or wait for other CPAN to test for
    me if I don't get the time to do it myself....))) but
    it was the default version of module-starter and it seems
    like a good place to start.  (Better than v5.12, that's for
    sure... https://redirect.github.com/rra/podlators/issues/35)

